# ARCH-0V Tranche 2 — encoding normalisation.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# At ARCH-22 completion, `backend/requirements.txt` and
# `backend/requirements-dev.txt` were UTF-16LE with a byte-order mark, and
# `backend/app/schemas/usage.py` carried a UTF-8 BOM. All three are the
# signature of PowerShell redirection (`pip freeze > requirements.txt` writes
# UTF-16LE on Windows) landing in the repository without normalisation.
#
# The consequences were not cosmetic:
#
#   * Every SCA scanner — Dependabot, pip-audit, and whatever an enterprise
#     buyer's security review runs — opens requirements.txt as UTF-8 and sees
#     either nothing or garbage. A platform with 177 pinned dependencies
#     reporting zero declared dependencies is a procurement finding.
#   * `ast.parse(open(path, encoding="utf-8"))` raises SyntaxError on a BOM'd
#     source file, which is why every static gate in the repository has been
#     paying an `encoding="utf-8-sig"` tax since ARCH-19.
#
# Fixing the three files once is not enough. The authoring path that produced
# them is still there. This file is the mechanism; `verify_arch0v.py` checks
# G3 and G4 are the enforcement.

# Default: Git decides what is text, and normalises it to LF in the index.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit text declarations for the file types that matter most here, so a
# `core.autocrlf=true` Windows checkout cannot reintroduce CRLF into the index.
*.py      text eol=lf
*.pyi     text eol=lf
*.ts      text eol=lf
*.tsx     text eol=lf
*.js      text eol=lf
*.jsx     text eol=lf
*.mjs     text eol=lf
*.cjs     text eol=lf
*.json    text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
*.toml    text eol=lf
*.cfg     text eol=lf
*.ini     text eol=lf
*.sql     text eol=lf
*.css     text eol=lf
*.html    text eol=lf
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.txt     text eol=lf
*.env.example text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
Makefile  text eol=lf
.gitignore text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Cron files are read by cron, which is unforgiving about line endings.
deploy/cron.d/* text eol=lf

# Binary: never touched, never normalised, never diffed as text.
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.gif     binary
*.webp    binary
*.ico     binary
*.pdf     binary
*.zip     binary
*.gz      binary
*.woff    binary
*.woff2   binary
*.ttf     binary
*.eot     binary
*.onnx    binary
*.bin     binary
*.pt      binary
*.safetensors binary

# Lockfiles are generated; collapse them in reviews so a 40,000-line diff does
# not bury the two lines that matter.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff
yarn.lock         linguist-generated=true -diff
